.TH ANONSURF 1 "July 2026" "AnonSurf 6.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anonsurf \- anonymization toolkit for Parrot Security OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anonsurf
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AnonSurf
manages system-wide Tor transparent routing on Parrot Security OS.
It provides commands to start and stop the AnonSurf service, inspect
runtime status, request a new Tor identity, check the public Tor status,
and manage startup integration.
.PP
The Go command-line interface keeps
.B anonsurf status
scriptable. Interactive Tor monitoring is available separately through
.B anonsurf monitor
or
.B anonsurf status --nyx.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start [--safe-kill]
Start system-wide Tor transparent routing. When
.B --safe-kill
is supplied, AnonSurf runs
.B /usr/lib/anonsurf/safekill
before changing service state.
.TP
.B stop [--safe-kill]
Stop AnonSurf and return to clearnet. When
.B --safe-kill
is supplied, AnonSurf runs
.B /usr/lib/anonsurf/safekill
before changing service state.
.TP
.B restart [--safe-kill]
Restart AnonSurf routing. When
.B --safe-kill
is supplied, AnonSurf runs
.B /usr/lib/anonsurf/safekill
before changing service state.
.TP
.B status
Print a read-only snapshot of AnonSurf service state, Tor service state,
DNS classification, and configured DNS servers.
.TP
.B status --nyx
Open Nyx using the AnonSurf configuration instead of printing the
scriptable status snapshot.
.TP
.B monitor
Open Nyx using
.B /etc/anonsurf/nyxrc.
.TP
.B changeid
Request a new Tor identity through Tor's control port.
.TP
.B newnym
Alias for
.B changeid.
.TP
.B myip
Check the current public IP address and whether it is seen as Tor traffic.
.TP
.B ip
Alias for
.B myip.
.TP
.B enable-boot
Enable AnonSurf at system startup.
.TP
.B disable-boot
Disable AnonSurf at system startup.
.TP
.B status-boot
Show whether AnonSurf is enabled at startup.
.SH RELATED TOOLS
.TP
.B dnstool
Manage and inspect system DNS settings used by AnonSurf.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/anonsurf/make-torrc
Generate or restore Tor configuration from AnonSurf settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/anonsurf/anonsurf.cfg
AnonSurf configuration.
.TP
.B /etc/anonsurf/bridges.txt
Bridge list used when automatic bridge selection is enabled.
.TP
.B /etc/anonsurf/nyxrc
Nyx configuration used by
.B anonsurf monitor
and
.B anonsurf status --nyx.
.TP
.B /etc/tor/torrc
Tor configuration generated by AnonSurf.
.TP
.B /var/lib/anonsurf/torrc.backup
Backup of the previous Tor configuration.
.SH AUTHORS
AnonSurf was developed by the Parrot Security team and contributors.
.PP
